LeRobot
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes software derived from LeRobot 0.4.4
(https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.
Copyright 2024-2025 Tony Z. Zhao and The HuggingFace Inc. team.

Modified copies of LeRobot 0.4.4 files in this repository:

  submission/policy/modeling_act.py
    Copy of lerobot policies/act/modeling_act.py (LeRobot 0.4.4), used by
    LiftPot's model. Changes (20 lines): the import block is replaced by
    constants and stubs, and a latent_override hook was added for an optional
    inference mode (not enabled for any task). Apart from a 6-line comment
    with this change notice, it is byte-identical to the submitted file
    (SHA-1 9d869c7d...).

  training/policy_v2/modeling_act.py
    Copy of the same file, used by the GRPO code. Changes (17 lines): the
    import block only.

The model weights were trained with the unmodified LeRobot 0.4.4 package.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RoboEval
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product uses RoboEval (https://robo-eval.github.io/challenge.html) at the
git tag corl2026-challenge (commit c8b79598c9fb9021652128020517d1847abe4c95)
as an external dependency for simulation and evaluation. No RoboEval source
file is included here. RoboEval is released under the MIT License (its README
says "licensed under the MIT License", and the challenge organizers confirmed
MIT); its repository's LICENSE file holds the Apache-2.0 text. MuJoCo and
MuJoCo Menagerie (both Apache-2.0) are used through RoboEval and are not
included here either.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data derived from RoboEval assets (hand-designed controllers)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two data files in submission/policy/ are derived from object assets released
with RoboEval (same tag; MIT License, see above):

  submission/policy/rv_valve_pts.npy
    21,911 surface points sampled from the valve meshes
    roboeval/envs/xmls/props/garage/handwheel_valve/assets/base_link.stl and
    valve.stl (area-weighted samples, 2.5 mm voxel grid, valve root frame).

  submission/policy/tray_mesh.npz
    The visual mesh of roboeval/envs/xmls/props/breakfast_tray/assets/
    wood_tray.obj (SHA-1 8b5663d29fd81b93e008b84da1037ddb0a46b0a1), 744
    vertices and 548 triangles, scaled by 1.1 as in wood_tray.xml and written
    in the tray body frame.

The controller code also contains numeric constants read once, during
development, from the released RoboEval scene and asset descriptions (camera
poses and field of view, table, counter, shelf and box geometry, object
sizes, centres of mass, spawn ranges) and from the Franka Emika Panda
description of MuJoCo Menagerie shipped with RoboEval (gripper and hand
dimensions, joint ranges; Apache-2.0). No file of either is copied.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RoboEval demonstrations
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The LiftPot model was trained on the RoboEval demonstrations: Hugging Face
dataset helen9975/roboeval_ee_delta_20hz_scaled, revision
918b4072cd1d15f28b1f96a440ac7aa84591ce92. The demonstrations are not included
in this repository. The dataset repository has no dataset card and no license
tag; the challenge page (https://robo-eval.github.io/challenge.html) states
the license as MIT and says the "benchmark, assets, and demonstrations are
free to use".

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pretrained backbone
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The ACT backbone was initialized from torchvision's ResNet-18 ImageNet weights
(IMAGENET1K_V1), distributed with torchvision (BSD license). ImageNet's own
terms apply to the ImageNet dataset.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Differences from the submitted bundle
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

submission/metadata.yaml is the submitted metadata without the contact
e-mail. The downloaded LiftPot config.json and train_config.json have local
paths replaced by ~/... (fields the policy never reads). With the
modeling_act.py notice above, these are the only differences: every other
file, including the weights, is byte-identical to the submission.
